      "role": "user",
      "content": "it’s just so quiet here. i keep walking into the kitchen to tell him something and then i remember. the house feels so empty it actually hurts to breathe sometimes. i don't know how people just keep going like nothing happened.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'm so sorry—that kind of silence is a weight no one should carry alone. Grief doesn't follow a timeline, and the fact that your body still expects him is proof of how deeply you loved him. It's okay to let the emptiness be loud; you don't have to \"keep going\" the way others expect. Just breathe, one moment at a time, and know that the ache itself is a form of love that hasn't finished speaking.",
